    "markdown": "![Hugging Face's logo](https://huggingface.co/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face⟨1⟩\n  *  Models ⟨2⟩\n  *  Datasets ⟨3⟩\n  *  Spaces ⟨4⟩\n  *  Buckets new⟨5⟩\n  *  Docs ⟨6⟩\n  *  Enterprise ⟨7⟩\n  * Pricing⟨8⟩\n  *     * Website\n      *  Tasks⟨9⟩\n      *  HuggingChat⟨10⟩\n      *  Collections⟨11⟩\n      *  Languages⟨12⟩\n      *  Organizations⟨13⟩\n    * Community\n      *  Blog⟨14⟩\n      *  Posts⟨15⟩\n      *  Daily Papers⟨16⟩\n      *  Hardware⟨17⟩\n      *  Learn⟨18⟩\n      *  Discord⟨19⟩\n      *  Forum⟨20⟩\n      *  GitHub⟨21⟩\n    * Solutions\n      *  Team & Enterprise⟨7⟩\n      *  Hugging Face PRO⟨22⟩\n      *  Enterprise Support⟨23⟩\n      *  Inference Providers⟨24⟩\n      *  Inference Endpoints⟨25⟩\n      *  Storage Buckets⟨5⟩\n  * * * *\n  * Log In⟨26⟩\n  * Sign Up⟨27⟩\n\n\n#   Datasets:⟨3⟩\n* * *\n ![](https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/1666181274838-62fa1d95e8c9c532aa75331c.png) ⟨28⟩\nAIML-TUDA⟨28⟩\n/\nClimbMix-split⟨29⟩\nlike 0\nFollow\n![⟨30⟩] Artificial Intelligence & Machine Learning Lab at TU Darmstadt 94\nTasks:  Text Generation ⟨31⟩\nModalities:  Tabular ⟨32⟩ Text ⟨33⟩\nFormats:  json ⟨34⟩\nLanguages:  English ⟨35⟩\nSize:  100M - 1B ⟨36⟩\nLibraries:  Datasets ⟨37⟩ Dask ⟨38⟩ Polars ⟨39⟩ + 1\nLicense:\nother\n Dataset card ⟨29⟩ Data Studio ⟨40⟩ Files Files and versions xet ⟨41⟩ Community ⟨42⟩\n##  You need to agree to share your contact information to access this dataset\nThis repository is publicly accessible, but you have to accept the conditions to access its files and content.\nLog in⟨43⟩ or Sign Up⟨44⟩ to review the conditions and access this dataset content.\n  * Splits⟨45⟩\n  * Schema⟨46⟩\n  * Matching Method⟨47⟩\n  * Terms And Provenance⟨48⟩\n\n\n#   ⟨49⟩ ClimbMix Split \n`climbmix-split` reorganizes the detokenized NVIDIA ClimbMix source corpus into source-oriented splits. ClimbMix is described as being built from Nemotron-CC and SmolLM-Corpus. Because SmolLM-Corpus is the smaller and directly identifiable component, we used exact normalized-text matching against SmolLM-Corpus to recover the SmolLM-derived portions. The remaining rows are provided as the residual `nemotron-cc` split.\nThe data rows are unchanged from the detokenized ClimbMix source. Only the shard placement changes.\n##   ⟨45⟩ Splits   \n| Split  | Rows  | Meaning  |  \n| --- | --- | --- |  \n| `nemotron-cc`  | 509,811,042  | ClimbMix rows with no exact normalized-text match in the configured SmolLM-Corpus subsets.  |  \n| `fineweb-edu-dedup`  | 34,057,577  | Rows exact-matching `HuggingFaceTB/smollm-corpus` config `fineweb-edu-dedup`.  |  \n| `cosmopedia-v2`  | 9,139,988  | Rows exact-matching `HuggingFaceTB/smollm-corpus` config `cosmopedia-v2`.  |  \n| `python-edu`  | 306,449  | Rows exact-matching `HuggingFaceTB/smollm-corpus` config `python-edu`.  |  \nThe `nemotron-cc` split is a residual split with respect to this exact-match run. It should not be read as proof that a row has no overlap with any other external corpus.\n##   ⟨46⟩ Schema \nEach row is JSONL with:\n  * `cluster_id`: integer ClimbMix cluster assignment\n  * `text`: detokenized source text\n  * `token_count`: source token count from ClimbMix metadata\n\n\n##   ⟨47⟩ Matching Method \nThe split was derived with exact normalized-text matching between ClimbMix rows and the SmolLM-Corpus subsets:\n  * `fineweb-edu-dedup`\n  * `cosmopedia-v2`\n  * `python-edu`\n\n\nText was normalized with:\n  * Unicode NFKC normalization\n  * line-ending normalization\n  * trimming at text edges\n  * whitespace collapse\n  * 128-bit BLAKE2b over normalized UTF-8 text, paired with normalized byte length\n\n\n`python-edu` text was resolved from the SmolLM metadata using the Software Heritage blob content flow described by the SmolLM-Corpus dataset card.\nRows with a match to exactly one configured SmolLM-Corpus subset were assigned to that source split. Rows with no configured SmolLM-Corpus match were assigned to `nemotron-cc`. The uploaded `metadata/source_membership.parquet` stores one row per matched ClimbMix ID with its matched source membership, primary split label, and multi-source flag.\n##   ⟨48⟩ Terms And Provenance \nThis dataset is marked as `other` on Hugging Face because the split labels are source-provenance labels, and the relevant upstream terms differ by split. The matched splits expose additional source context from SmolLM-Corpus, FineWeb-Edu, Cosmopedia, and The Stack v2; the residual split remains tied to the ClimbMix/Nemotron-CC source context.\nSee `LICENSE.md` for the split-specific terms notice and `metadata/source_license_pointers.json` for machine-readable source pointers.\nPrimary source pointers:\n  * ClimbMix: <https://huggingface.co/datasets/nvidia/Nemotron-ClimbMix>\n  * SmolLM-Corpus: <https://huggingface.co/datasets/HuggingFaceTB/smollm-corpus>\n  * FineWeb-Edu: <https://huggingface.co/datasets/HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-edu>\n  * Cosmopedia: <https://huggingface.co/datasets/HuggingFaceTB/cosmopedia>\n  * The Stack v2: <https://huggingface.co/datasets/bigcode/the-stack-v2>\n  * Nemotron-CC-v2: <https://huggingface.co/datasets/nvidia/Nemotron-CC-v2>\n\n\nThis README is provenance documentation, not legal advice. Check upstream dataset cards and terms before redistribution or training use.\nCopy to bucket new \n\nDownloads last month\n    373\nTotal file size: 1.69 TB\n##  Collection including AIML-TUDA/ClimbMix-split\n#### KletterMix Collection 6 items • Updated 12 days ago • 6 ⟨50⟩\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨51⟩ Privacy⟨52⟩ About⟨53⟩ Careers⟨54⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\n",
